TI  - Hospital architectural spatial knowledge graph: Incremental development and scenario-based applications enabled by generative AI and building information modeling
T2  - ENGINEERING APPLICATIONS OF ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE
AB  - Hospital architectural design requires integrating heterogeneous information under complex and evolving regulatory constraints, yet conventional experience-driven workflows remain time-consuming and difficult to trace. This study develops a hospital architectural spatial knowledge graph (AS-KG) framework for the structured organization, controlled updating, retrieval, and application of hospital design-code knowledge. Grounded in authoritative hospital regulations, the framework integrates corpus development, information extraction, graph construction, controlled knowledge updating, knowledge-enhanced question answering, and building information modeling (BIM)-assisted compliance checking. On an independent held-out set, the incremental expansion workflow improved triple precision from 75.00% at the raw extraction stage to 98.21%. In the questionanswering benchmark, the full knowledge graph (KG)-enhanced setting correctly covered 263 of 283 key points (92.9%), outperforming both the implemented text-based RAG baseline and general large language model (LLM)-only baseline. In a selected outpatient-floor BIM case, the module achieved an agreement rate of 92.8% among the checked rule instances. Together, these results demonstrate the feasibility and practical value of a hospital-oriented knowledge engineering workflow for structured regulatory knowledge organization, evidencegrounded retrieval, and case-based design review.
