AU  - Meddeb, A
AU  - Ben Romdhane, L
TI  - Single and multi-graph orchestration in recommendation systems: A systematic literature review
T2  - ENGINEERING APPLICATIONS OF ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE
AB  - The rise of Web 2.0 has led to the creation and sharing of vast amounts of content through social media and collaborative platforms, resulting in an overwhelming amount of online data. This abundance of information has made it difficult for users to find relevant content. Recommendation systems (RS) address this challenge by suggesting content that aligns with users' preferences and behaviors, enhancing user experience and boosting engagement. To effectively learn user preferences and provide personalized recommendations, it is essential to capture the underlying relationships within the data. Knowledge graph (KG)-based methods provide promising solutions by capturing semantic relationships and contextual information between entities such as users and items. This paper presents a systematic literature review (SLR) of knowledge graph-based recommender systems (KG-based RS). We introduce a novel classification framework for KG-based RS models based on their architectural design, distinguishing between single-graph and multi-graph-based architectures, which are further divided into sub-categories. We also explore the application of these models across various domains and discuss the key challenges and future research directions in the field.
